{"vid":"mcvqpfOaSuo","source":"mcvqpfOaSuo.en.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0,"txt":"SCOTT ANTHONY: 1453, an army approaches Constantinople."},{"t":4.9,"txt":"If you're inside the walls of Constantinople,"},{"t":7.9,"txt":"you probably feel OK, because after all,"},{"t":10.6,"txt":"those walls had stood for more than 1,000 years."},{"t":14,"txt":"There's a literal moat that goes around the city."},{"t":17,"txt":"Once you get past the moat, you get to two sets"},{"t":19.7,"txt":"of walls, each 18 feet thick."},{"t":22.6,"txt":"Those walls were impenetrable before."},{"t":26.4,"txt":"Saltpeter, sulfur, charcoal, three ingredients that,"},{"t":30,"txt":"when combined in the right way, created gunpowder."},{"t":32.8,"txt":"First identified in about 142."},{"t":36.6,"txt":"1,300 years later, a mysterious figure named Orban appears."},{"t":42.1,"txt":"He goes to the people inside the walls, the Byzantine Empire,"},{"t":45.7,"txt":"and says, I can sell you something"},{"t":48,"txt":"that will protect your city."},{"t":50,"txt":"The Byzantine Empire passes."},{"t":52.4,"txt":"Orban goes to the Ottoman Empire that is seeking to sack the city"},{"t":56.5,"txt":"and makes the same proposition."},{"t":58,"txt":"They say yes."},{"t":59.3,"txt":"Imagine how it felt. Walls that had stood for 1,000 years faced"},{"t":63.9,"txt":"the onslaught of a half ton cannonball flung over"},{"t":68,"txt":"the distance of a mile."},{"t":69.6,"txt":"The walls shattered."},{"t":71.2,"txt":"The city fell in 47 days."},{"t":74.1,"txt":"Disruption changes everything."},{"t":77.1,"txt":"The question you have to ask in modern times"},{"t":79.5,"txt":"is, what is the moat that we have, that we built yesterday,"},{"t":83.2,"txt":"that might protect us today, but will"},{"t":85.7,"txt":"be powerless against the disruptions in the future?"},{"t":90.8,"txt":"Why is it that market leaders pass on disruptive innovations?"},{"t":94.9,"txt":"Well, when you first see a disruptive innovation,"},{"t":97.6,"txt":"it looks really different."},{"t":99,"txt":"It looks unfamiliar, and therefore, it's"},{"t":101.4,"txt":"pretty easy to discount it."},{"t":103.1,"txt":"If you're inside walls that had stood for 1,000 years and you"},{"t":107.4,"txt":"see this unproven canon present in front of you,"},{"t":111,"txt":"you don't fully understand it."},{"t":112.8,"txt":"You don't fully see its use."},{"t":114.4,"txt":"You're used to horses."},{"t":115.9,"txt":"You're used to cavalry."},{"t":117.1,"txt":"You're used to arrows."},{"t":118.4,"txt":"Those are things that had worked for a very long period of time."},{"t":121.9,"txt":"It's only once you see the full demonstration"},{"t":125.3,"txt":"of the power of the disruption that you really, truly get it."},{"t":130.6,"txt":"Why historically have disruptive innovations"},{"t":133.3,"txt":"tended to start with upstarts?"},{"t":135.5,"txt":"Well, Bob Dylan put it pretty well."},{"t":137.3,"txt":"When you ain't got nothing, you got nothing to lose."},{"t":139.4,"txt":"A market leader sees a downside."},{"t":142.1,"txt":"They see risks."},{"t":143.1,"txt":"They see threats."},{"t":144,"txt":"Somebody who is an upstart sees nothing"},{"t":146.3,"txt":"but gain and possibility."},{"t":148.2,"txt":"So therefore, it's pretty natural"},{"t":150.7,"txt":"that an upstart will go and gravitate"},{"t":153.1,"txt":"to following a new disruptive approach."},{"t":155.6,"txt":"And the research shows that's a smart thing to do."},{"t":158.3,"txt":"If you try to take on the incumbent in a battle"},{"t":161.6,"txt":"that they are used to playing and you try to do it better,"},{"t":164.6,"txt":"they're going to beat you most of the time."},{"t":166.3,"txt":"Clay Christensen called that a sustaining innovation battle."},{"t":169.9,"txt":"If you try to take them on with a very different form of battle,"},{"t":174.2,"txt":"you've got a much greater chance of winning."},{"t":176.3,"txt":"So it's natural that if you don't go and counteract"},{"t":179.4,"txt":"these forces, the upstart's going"},{"t":181.4,"txt":"to see it and jump all over it."},{"t":183.1,"txt":"The incumbent is going to hesitate and pause."},{"t":188.4,"txt":"When you look at a new innovation,"},{"t":190.5,"txt":"it always feels like there's risk involved."},{"t":192.7,"txt":"So you have to make a decision."},{"t":194.4,"txt":"Am I going to put a dollar, euro, rupee, whatever"},{"t":197.6,"txt":"into this innovation or that innovation?"},{"t":200.7,"txt":"One of the big challenges a market leader"},{"t":202.8,"txt":"has is a comparison."},{"t":205,"txt":"Should I spend that unit of resource making today better,"},{"t":208.7,"txt":"or should I spend it making tomorrow different?"},{"t":211.4,"txt":"If you're a company that's got nothing,"},{"t":213.4,"txt":"you only think about what do I do that's going"},{"t":216.1,"txt":"to have the maximum impact?"},{"t":217.5,"txt":"You look for the most exciting things, the things with the most"},{"t":220.1,"txt":"potential."},{"t":220.9,"txt":"Your resources naturally allocate towards the disruption."},{"t":224.9,"txt":"This is the rational part of the innovator's dilemma."},{"t":228.5,"txt":"Left unchecked, the resource allocation process"},{"t":232.1,"txt":"inside an organization will direct everything to the known,"},{"t":237,"txt":"to the proven, to the things that appear to be safe,"},{"t":239.7,"txt":"not recognizing that you're actually taking a risk by not"},{"t":244.4,"txt":"taking a risk, by leaving yourself"},{"t":246.7,"txt":"susceptible to somebody who comes at you"},{"t":249.2,"txt":"with a disruptive innovation."}],"words":[{"t":0,"w":"SCOTT"},{"t":0,"w":"ANTHONY:"},{"t":0,"w":"1453,"},{"t":0,"w":"an"},{"t":0,"w":"army"},{"t":0,"w":"approaches"},{"t":0,"w":"Constantinople."},{"t":4.89,"w":"If"},{"t":4.89,"w":"you're"},{"t":4.89,"w":"inside"},{"t":4.89,"w":"the"},{"t":4.89,"w":"walls"},{"t":4.89,"w":"of"},{"t":4.89,"w":"Constantinople,"},{"t":7.92,"w":"you"},{"t":7.92,"w":"probably"},{"t":7.92,"w":"feel"},{"t":7.92,"w":"OK,"},{"t":7.92,"w":"because"},{"t":7.92,"w":"after"},{"t":7.92,"w":"all,"},{"t":10.56,"w":"those"},{"t":10.56,"w":"walls"},{"t":10.56,"w":"had"},{"t":10.56,"w":"stood"},{"t":10.56,"w":"for"},{"t":10.56,"w":"more"},{"t":10.56,"w":"than"},{"t":10.56,"w":"1,000"},{"t":10.56,"w":"years."},{"t":14.01,"w":"There's"},{"t":14.01,"w":"a"},{"t":14.01,"w":"literal"},{"t":14.01,"w":"moat"},{"t":14.01,"w":"that"},{"t":14.01,"w":"goes"},{"t":14.01,"w":"around"},{"t":14.01,"w":"the"},{"t":14.01,"w":"city."},{"t":17.01,"w":"Once"},{"t":17.01,"w":"you"},{"t":17.01,"w":"get"},{"t":17.01,"w":"past"},{"t":17.01,"w":"the"},{"t":17.01,"w":"moat,"},{"t":17.01,"w":"you"},{"t":17.01,"w":"get"},{"t":17.01,"w":"to"},{"t":17.01,"w":"two"},{"t":17.01,"w":"sets"},{"t":19.73,"w":"of"},{"t":19.73,"w":"walls,"},{"t":19.73,"w":"each"},{"t":19.73,"w":"18"},{"t":19.73,"w":"feet"},{"t":19.73,"w":"thick."},{"t":22.55,"w":"Those"},{"t":22.55,"w":"walls"},{"t":22.55,"w":"were"},{"t":22.55,"w":"impenetrable"},{"t":22.55,"w":"before."},{"t":26.39,"w":"Saltpeter,"},{"t":26.39,"w":"sulfur,"},{"t":26.39,"w":"charcoal,"},{"t":26.39,"w":"three"},{"t":26.39,"w":"ingredients"},{"t":26.39,"w":"that,"},{"t":29.97,"w":"when"},{"t":29.97,"w":"combined"},{"t":29.97,"w":"in"},{"t":29.97,"w":"the"},{"t":29.97,"w":"right"},{"t":29.97,"w":"way,"},{"t":29.97,"w":"created"},{"t":29.97,"w":"gunpowder."},{"t":32.79,"w":"First"},{"t":32.79,"w":"identified"},{"t":32.79,"w":"in"},{"t":32.79,"w":"about"},{"t":32.79,"w":"142."},{"t":36.57,"w":"1,300"},{"t":36.57,"w":"years"},{"t":36.57,"w":"later,"},{"t":36.57,"w":"a"},{"t":36.57,"w":"mysterious"},{"t":36.57,"w":"figure"},{"t":36.57,"w":"named"},{"t":36.57,"w":"Orban"},{"t":36.57,"w":"appears."},{"t":42.09,"w":"He"},{"t":42.09,"w":"goes"},{"t":42.09,"w":"to"},{"t":42.09,"w":"the"},{"t":42.09,"w":"people"},{"t":42.09,"w":"inside"},{"t":42.09,"w":"the"},{"t":42.09,"w":"walls,"},{"t":42.09,"w":"the"},{"t":42.09,"w":"Byzantine"},{"t":42.09,"w":"Empire,"},{"t":45.